      "id": "1d847ec9-c379-5013-ab77-a9b92dc8ca27",
      "title": "Identifying the Matrix With a Given Rank by Inspection"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "f3f69b6a-d956-5c12-9020-408d61389e87",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following matrices have a rank of $6?$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 5 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 7 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 & 2 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 4 & 7 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that a matrix of rank $6$ must have at least $6$ columns and at least $6$ rows. \nSo, we disregard the matrix $A$ since it has only $5$ columns and the matrix $B$ since it has only $4$ columns.\n\nAlso, the matrix must have $6$ pivot columns. As we can see, the matrix $C$ has only $5$ pivot columns. So, $\\text{rank}(C)=5.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\"",
