      ":question/id": "cfe5e2ca-f817-59ef-b246-b8e3056fc853",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the numbers below belong to $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$ is the set of all negative rational numbers.\n\n- $\\sqrt{46}$: It is positive, and it is an irrational real number. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$.\n\n- $\\sqrt{48}=4\\sqrt{3}$: It is positive, and it is an irrational real number. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$.\n\n- $-3\\sqrt{6}$: It is negative, and it is an irrational real number. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$.\n\n- $0$: Zero is not negative or positive, and this set does not include zero. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is: None of those listed.",
